{"authored" [{"question" "q-140043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x+5y-3z=2 \\\\ 4x-5y+kz=1 \\\\ -2x+10y-5z=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that  $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $160-70k,$ find the value of $k.$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-140043/review.json" "file_sha256" "60b15e5635e785be088411e8c6ef5f6620ac0cffecad42a3285df7927822fef5" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-140043/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "ded74c931e15435511c2914064233bd56369df69e08f507697f9bb503afdfc92" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-140043/verification.json" "basis" 1920 "rationale" "Correct only the first coefficient determinant matrix row from 6,5,-2 to 6,5,-3. The unchanged prompt has coefficient -3 for z; the unchanged determinant 160-70k, Dx=75-30k and accepted key k=1 all use that correct coefficient. The original screenshot and accessible MathML confirm the source displays -2, excluding an extraction issue. Preserve raw captures, solver evidence, choices, answer fields and identities, accepted key, and historical versions."} {"question" "q-140043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}6 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -5 & k \\\\ -2 & 10 & -5\\end{aligned}|=160-70k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -5 & k \\\\ -2 & 10 & -5\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-5 & k \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{aligned}|-5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & k \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}|+(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(25-10k)-5(-5+2k)-3(10-10) \\\\  & =50-20k+25-10k+0 \\\\  & =75-30k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{75-30k}{160-70k}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{75-30k}{160-70k} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2(75-30k) & =160-70k \\\\ 150-60k & =160-70k \\\\ 10k & =10 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-140043/review.json" "file_sha256" "60b15e5635e785be088411e8c6ef5f6620ac0cffecad42a3285df7927822fef5" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-140043/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "ded74c931e15435511c2914064233bd56369df69e08f507697f9bb503afdfc92" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-140043/verification.json" "basis" 1920 "rationale" "Correct only the first coefficient determinant matrix row from 6,5,-2 to 6,5,-3. The unchanged prompt has coefficient -3 for z; the unchanged determinant 160-70k, Dx=75-30k and accepted key k=1 all use that correct coefficient. The original screenshot and accessible MathML confirm the source displays -2, excluding an extraction issue. Preserve raw captures, solver evidence, choices, answer fields and identities, accepted key, and historical versions."} {"question" "q-140043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=1"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-140043/review.json" "file_sha256" "60b15e5635e785be088411e8c6ef5f6620ac0cffecad42a3285df7927822fef5" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-140043/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "ded74c931e15435511c2914064233bd56369df69e08f507697f9bb503afdfc92" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-140043/verification.json" "basis" 1920 "rationale" "Correct only the first coefficient determinant matrix row from 6,5,-2 to 6,5,-3. The unchanged prompt has coefficient -3 for z; the unchanged determinant 160-70k, Dx=75-30k and accepted key k=1 all use that correct coefficient. The original screenshot and accessible MathML confirm the source displays -2, excluding an extraction issue. Preserve raw captures, solver evidence, choices, answer fields and identities, accepted key, and historical versions."} {"question" "q-73686" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3y-2z=4 \\\\ -2x-3y=-6 \\\\ x+4z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}$, where $D$ is the determinant of the coefficient matrix and ${D}_{y}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "90e660673bc166676e860f53e1bf78c96bb1957df35ab66fba72bf7ee76dd251" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73686" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0x+3y+(-2)z=4 \\\\ (-2)x+(-3)y+0z=-6 \\\\ 1x+0y+4z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\nD=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned