eld" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "90e660673bc166676e860f53e1bf78c96bb1957df35ab66fba72bf7ee76dd251" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-139985" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "90e660673bc166676e860f53e1bf78c96bb1957df35ab66fba72bf7ee76dd251" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-139985" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 14 \\\\ -5 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "90e660673bc166676e860f53e1bf78c96bb1957df35ab66fba72bf7ee76dd251" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y-z=1 \\\\ x-2y+2z=3 \\\\ 3x-2y+z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $5,$ then $x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "90e660673bc166676e860f53e1bf78c96bb1957df35ab66fba72bf7ee76dd251" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+1y+(-1)z=1 \\\\ 1x+(-2)y+2z=3 \\\\ 3x+(-2)y+1z=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2-(-4))-(3-4)-(-6-(-4)) \\\\  & =2+1+2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{5}{5}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "90e660673bc166676e860f53e1bf78c96bb1957df35ab66fba72bf7ee76dd251" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/questio