ence/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1x+1y+3z=-2 \\\\ 2x+(-1)y+0z=3 \\\\ (-1)x+(-2)y+1z=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(-1-0)-(3-0)-(-6+6) \\\\  & =2-3-0 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{-1}{-18}=\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "90e660673bc166676e860f53e1bf78c96bb1957df35ab66fba72bf7ee76dd251" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linea