ficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|=66\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{y},$ we take the coefficients matrix, replace the second column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -10 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-10 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -10 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(20+1)+2(-4-2)+2(-2+20) \\\\  & =42-12+36 \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{66}{66}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "90e660673bc166676e860f53e1bf78c96bb1957df35ab66fba72bf7ee76dd251" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-139987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-139987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "90e660673bc166676e860f53e1bf78c96bb1957df35ab66fba72bf7