er/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-139987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "90e660673bc166676e860f53e1bf78c96bb1957df35ab66fba72bf7ee76dd251" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-139987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "90e660673bc166676e860f53e1bf78c96bb1957df35ab66fba72bf7ee76dd251" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y-z=1 \\\\ x+4y+kz=-1 \\\\ 2x+3y+4z=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that  $z=1$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $97-21k,$ find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "90e660673bc166676e860f53e1bf78c96bb1957df35ab66fba72bf7ee76dd251" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|=97-21k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $z$ is given by $z=\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}| & =5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{aligned}|-(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5(36+3)+3(9+2)+(3-8) \\\\  & =195+33-5 \\\\  & =223.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}=\\frac{223}{97-21k}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $z=1.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{223}{97-21k} & =1 \\\\ 223 & =97-21k \\\\ 21k & =-126 \\\\ k & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "90e660673bc166676e860f53e1bf78c96bb1957df35ab66fba72bf7ee76dd251" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4" "basis" 1914 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "90e660673bc166676e860f5